    "notes": "Puduhepa is independently attested as Hattusili III's queen. A seal on the 1259 BCE peace treaty with Ramesses II identifies her, and surviving Hittite material also preserves her diplomatic correspondence. ATLAS uses the treaty year as a bounded representative political-diplomatic milestone rather than inventing a full queenly tenure."
